                            displayMode="singleText"
                            elementNames="itinerary"
                            fragmentPath="/content/dam/weekender-shared/en/adventures/cycling-tuscany/cycling-tuscany"
                            paragraphScope="range"
                            text="Cycling Tuscany Day 1: The Chianti hills From a village among the vineyards we ride south over rolling hills to Siena, entering the city through one of its medieval gates in time for an evening walk to the square. Day 2: Clay hills South of Siena the land opens into bare, pale ridges with a single farmhouse on each. A long gravel section leads to an abbey among the cypresses, and to dinner at a farm that makes its own pecorino. Day 3: Val d'Orcia The postcard day: a winding avenue of cypresses, a hot spring where you can soak tired legs, and a climb to a hill town known for its red wine. Day 4: Back through the vines A shorter ride on quiet roads to the last lunch, long and unhurried, before the transfer to Florence."
